    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d737">

                <pb facs="0791" n="781" sameAs="frus:frus1949v09/pg781"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.5151/5–2349: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Stuart</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-05-23T11:00:00+08:00">May 23, 1949—11 a.
                            m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received May 23—2:22 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1088. [To Hankow:] In accordance paragraph 2, Deptel 536, April 29<anchor n="92"
                        xml:id="d737-f1"/> to Embassy, sent Hankow as Embcirtel May 8, Embassy
                    concurs ConGen’s proposal comply surrender regulations if applied Hankow.
                    (Refurtel 103, May 12.<anchor n="93" xml:id="d737-f2"/>)</p>
                <p>Embassy wishes suggest however highly desirable that if possible total surrender
                    US dollars to be done under agreement with Communist bank authorities permitting
                    periodic ConGen withdrawals against US dollar credit at going rate day
                    withdrawal occurs. ConGen should keep in mind possible rapid depreciation lump
                    sum local currency exchanged for ConGen’s US dollars. Working and intent any
                    regulations issued should be carefully studied and ConGen should explore all
                    possible methods of conserving US dollar assets in light of regulations <pb
                        facs="0792" n="782" xml:id="pg782"/> and conditions existing locally at time
                    surrender problem arises.</p>
                <p>Sent Hankow 28, repeated Department 1088, passed Hankow.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stuart</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
